course: dictionary
lesson: 11879
title: Brainstorming
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes you need lots of ideas, and it is hard to find them all at once. Brainstorming is a way to do that. People say every idea that comes to mind, quickly, and nobody judges them. «Let's brainstorm names for the class pet.» The aim is to get lots of ideas on the board first, and to choose the best ones later.
explain: The rules matter. No idea is silly, so write everything down. Build on other people's ideas: «Yes, and we could add a picture to that!» Do not stop to argue. Brainstorming is about quantity first, and quality comes when you pick.
explain: You can use brainstorming as a noun or a verb. As a noun: «Our brainstorming gave us twenty ideas.» As a verb, with the -ing form: «We are brainstorming a plan for the school garden.» In both sentences, the word names the activity of finding ideas together.
fact: Brainstorming means finding lots of ideas quickly.
fact: «Brainstorming» can be a noun, as in «We had a brainstorming session», or a verb, as in «We are brainstorming titles».
fact: The main rules are: say every idea, do not judge any of them, and build on other people's ideas.
fact: Brainstorming is often done on a board or on sticky notes, so everyone can see the ideas.
fact: Choose the best ideas only after you have finished brainstorming.
exercise: «Before writing, we did brainstorming on sticky notes.» What is brainstorming here? | A test with marks at the end | A kind of drawing lesson | *A quick way of finding ideas, saying every idea without judging | Tidying up the classroom
exercise: What is a rule of brainstorming? | Keep your best idea secret | Judge each idea before anyone speaks | *Write everything down, even ideas that seem silly | Only say ideas you are sure will work
exercise: «Let's brainstorm a name for our club.» What kind of word is brainstorm in this sentence? | *A verb | A noun | A question word | An adjective
test: «Our brainstorming gave us twenty ideas for the school play.» What does brainstorming mean? | Writing a final copy of a story | Choosing one idea and checking it | *Quickly saying lots of ideas without judging them | Sitting quietly and thinking alone
test: Ella says, «Let's build on Sam's idea.» What does building on an idea mean in brainstorming? | Judging the idea as silly | Ignoring the idea | *Adding to someone else's idea | Writing the idea in a book for next year
exam: Why do people brainstorm before they start a project? | To finish the project at once | *To find lots of ideas, then choose the best | To stop others from speaking | To write the final copy
